<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-10> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/cell-geometry-thompson1917-ch07-10>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/cell-geometry-thompson1917-ch07-10> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/EvidenceItem>;
    <https://schema.org/value> 4;
    dc:description "Exploratory test of thompson1917-ch07-10: If close-packed cells of varying size are on average hexagonal, the mean number of neighbours of fully surrounded cells is 6.\n\nResult: 4 (usable tissues with mean neighbour number within 0.1 of 6; n = 5; one image per tissue).\n\nCriterion: Exploratory, not pre-registered: the images were segmented and inspected before the pass criterion was written. Treat the verdict as hypothesis-generating; a pre-registered replication on new images is needed before it counts as a test. A tissue conforms if its mean neighbour number is within 0.1 of 6. Supports if most usable tissues conform.\n\nInterpretation: Thompson's example is coral corallites; this tests the same statement on plant and animal cell sheets. Euler's formula forces a mean of 6 for any large planar tiling with three cells at every vertex, so agreement confirms the claim without testing a biological mechanism.";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Exploratory, not pre-registered: the images were segmented and inspected before the pass criterion was written. Treat the verdict as hypothesis-generating; a pre-registered replication on new images is needed before it counts as a test.\nA mean of 6 is a topological necessity for trivalent planar tilings (Euler), reproduced by the random-Voronoi control; it is not evidence for any biological mechanism.\nGrass epidermis falls short of 6, most likely because unsegmented stomata and hairs hide some neighbours.\nCorallites, Thompson's own example, were not tested.";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Exploratory cell-geometry test of thompson1917-ch07-10 on 5 images: supports";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/e66117b39b3f6cc9aadb3aac747d33176d47dd0d/claim-tests/thompson-growth-form/thompson1917-ch07-10/result.json>;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/wikimedia-commons-physcomitrella-leaf>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/wikimedia-commons-festuca-leaf-epidermis>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/wikimedia-commons-aloe-leaf-epidermis>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/wikimedia-commons-human-corneal-endothelium>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/wikimedia-commons-drosophila-compound-eye>;
    <https://schema.org/additionalProperty> sub:value0, sub:value1, sub:value10, sub:value11, sub:value12, sub:value13, sub:value14, sub:value15, sub:value16, sub:value17, sub:value18, sub:value19, sub:value2, sub:value20, sub:value21, sub:value3, sub:value4, sub:value5, sub:value6, sub:value7, sub:value8, sub:value9;
    <https://schema.org/unitText> "usable tissues with mean neighbour number within 0.1 of 6"
}
